  "notes": "Areas are drawn as broad shapes. Most are traced from maps of the Historical Dictionary of Switzerland (HLS: the Helvetii, the provinces in AD 14 and in the 4th century), matched to today's lakes (about 2 km off on average). Small tribe areas are drawn by hand. Far away from Switzerland, areas are drawn by hand as broad shapes. All ancient borders are only rough. Kinds are used for colour: 'roman' = the main Gaulish province of the Plateau (Belgica, Germania superior, Maxima Sequanorum), 'other' = Raetia, 'ally' = Alpes Graiae et Poeninae, 'noble' = Gallia Narbonensis, 'empire' = Italy; in step 2 'ally' = Raurici, 'noble' = Valais tribes, 'milan' = Lepontii. Negative years are BC.",
